  "room": "S11",
  "notes": "Dubravka tram stop, June 1995 morning (natural painting bg_natural/S11.webp): wind in the lindens left and right, clouds drifting behind the panel towers, the stop clock's red second hand ticking (the time node), pigeons pecking on the platform near the tram (they fly off when Adam comes close), now and then a small flock crossing the sky. The red-cream T3 (the exit to S19) is a sprite cut from the painting (art/ambient/natural/vehicles/build_s11.py): every 80 s it leaves towards the camera (accelerating), the track stays empty for 8 s and the next T3 comes in from the far end and brakes into the stop (16 s); tram_patch (the tramless track from one paid edit) covers the painted tram meanwhile. The chains are written by art/ambient/natural/vehicles/layers.py. Reduced motion hides all tram layers, so the painted tram stands still.",
